# API, Auth & React Query

## Axios instance

- Use only the default-export `axios` from `@src/requests` (token + refresh + i18n-error interceptors attached). Don't `import axios from "axios"` in feature code.
- `baseURL` from `window.__APP_CONFIG__.SITE_BASE_API_URL` (runtime config).
- Response generics: `IRes<T>` / `IResPagination<T>` / `IResData<T>` from `@src/models`.

## API module layout

```
src/requests/api/<domain>/
  <action>.ts            // get/post/put/delete functions
  prop-state.type.ts     // request/response interfaces (I...)
  index.ts               // optional re-export
```

Each file exports an object named `<domain>Requests` or `<domain>Middleware`:

```ts
const getUserInfo = async (params: IUserInfoParams) => {
  const response = await axios.get(`/products/${params.id}`);
  return response.data;
};
export const userRequests = { getUserInfo };
```

When adding a new domain, add `export * from "./<domain>"` to `src/requests/api/index.tsx`.

## Auth / Token

- Access token in cookie via `saveSessionId`/`getSessionId`/`removeSessionId` (`src/requests/token.ts`).
- Refresh token helpers in `src/requests/refresh-token.ts` (`sameSite: strict`, `secure: true`).
- Cookie names in `src/constants/cookies.constants.ts` (`ACCESS_TOKEN`, `REFRESH_TOKEN`, `expiresToken`).
- Don't call refresh-token from components; the interceptor handles it.

## React Query

- `QueryClient` configured in `src/App.tsx` (`refetchOnWindowFocus: false`, `retry: false`). Keep unless there's a clear reason.
- `queryKey` always from `EnumQueryKeys` (`src/enums/query.enum.ts`). Add new keys to the enum.
- Invalidate via `useInvalidateQuery(key)` from `@src/hooks`.

```ts
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: [EnumQueryKeys.EMPLOYEES_LIST, filter],
  queryFn: () => userRequests.getEmployees(filter),
});
const invalidate = useInvalidateQuery(EnumQueryKeys.EMPLOYEES_LIST);
```

## Date/time in payload

Use `dayjs` re-exported from `@src/utils` + `FORMAT_DATE` constants in `src/utils/datetime.ts` (e.g. `FORMAT_DATE.BE_DATE_TIME` for backend payloads).
